0. About this license

The purpose of this license is to allow reasonable, fair, and appropriate
sharing of resources among the community for a game or software project.

It's based on a loose interpretation of the GNU GPL v3 license and is designed
to promote a strong copyleft licensing system for game mods, while at the same
time preserving the hard work of mod authors and ensuring they are recognised
for their contributions.

Sharing is important for the health and quality of software communities, and
the general community at large, as it allows members to build upon the work of
others while ensuring that the members of the community all feel that their
hard work is being acknowledged while still allowing the free exchange of work
for the purposes of improving the quality of software overall.

This license is designed to create fair and equitable terms for mod authors,
while also ensuring players have the best access to the available work by the
community. It's designed to prevent "hoarding" while giving authors the
recognition they deserve, and allows people to contribute to projects for the
benefit of the community, whilst attempting to limit the ability of others to
join or otherwise wholesale adapt their work without recognition.

This license is designed to foster the Cathedral model outlined below, in which
mods are seen more as community works rather than individual, private works.
For more information on the philosophy of this modding license, see this
article:

https://wryemusings.com/Cathedral%20vs.%20Parlor.html

1. License Terms.

The software is provided under the following conditions:

Any user of this software may:
- Redistribute it in a binary form in part or in wholesale, as long as this
  license file is included with no modifications.
- Make adjustments or changes to the source code or assets for personal use without restriction
    - "Personal Use" refers to any use of the software that is not shared, published, or otherwise made accessible to others in any form.

Any user of the software may publicly release a modified version of the software,
or include it in other projects, under the following conditions:
- The resulting project is licensed under this license, with no modifications
- The resulting project, including it's source code and all related art and
  other assets, is publically accessible via an online service such as github,
  or hosted on a publicly-accessible online server in the form of a zip or other
  compressed archive that can be extracted using open-source, freely available
  tools such as 7-zip. The resulting project must be accessible freely and
  without restriction, and must not require any payment or other subscription or
  fee to access.
- The resulting project is not using LLMs such as Claude or AI code-generation
  tools for more than 5% of it's total codebase. This includes code analysis
  tools, AI assistants or LLM related toolchains that use machine learning models
  to directly or indirectly design, write, or provide instructions relating to
  modification of the resulting project code, art, or other assets.
- The resulting project may not be used for the purposes of weapons manufacture
  or control, AI training, or any military applications, including drone
  warfare.
- The creator of the original work must be credited in the readme or other
  credits file.

This project, and any resulting project, may not be used for the purposes of AI
training under any circumstances, including for the purposes of local-model or
self-hosted model training, nor may any AI agent or tool or LLM use code from
this project or any resulting project for any reason.

Additionally, this project may not be included in "mod packs" or other packaged
collections of works without explicit permission. A "mod pack" is defined as
any package or project containing work from other projects that does not make
substantial contributions or changes of it's own, such as adding major new
features.

